  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'To control the animations of the player, the PlayerAnimatorController
    uses the CharacterStatusProvider to retrieve information of the player''s current
    status, such as velocity or grounded status, and CharacterEventDispatcher to
    listen to events. These two classes act as single-point providers for all data
    needed by external systems, without having to reference all of the scripts and
    features attached to the player.


    The blocks implement interfaces such as
    ICeilingHitReceiver or IDashHitReceiver,  in order to react to multiple hit events
    by the player.'
